{
  "dom_id": "step-q124355",
  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "An angle $\\theta $ in the coordinate plane (measured in the usual way) has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{7}.$ Which of the following cannot be $\\theta ?$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's remind ourselves of the relationship between ${\\theta }_{R}$ and $\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14225277/assets/35e9a04cf71b42acdf7769ef541c5b93c9267130e965d52d3989f3a00692cea1.png)\n\nUsing ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{7},$ let's calculate all possible values of $\\theta .$\n\n- If $\\theta $ lies in the first quadrant, then $\\theta ={\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{7}.$\n\n- If $\\theta $ lies in the second quadrant, then $\\theta =\\pi -{\\theta }_{R}=\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{7}=\\frac{6\\pi }{7}.$\n\n- If $\\theta $ lies in the third quadrant, then $\\theta =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R}=\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{7}=\\frac{8\\pi }{7}.$\n\n- If $\\theta $ lies in the fourth quadrant, then $\\theta =2\\pi -{\\theta }_{R}=2\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{7}=\\frac{13\\pi }{7}.$\n\nTherefore, $\\theta $ cannot be equal to $\\frac{5\\pi }{7}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
